 "name": "Ignition",
 "type": "spell",
 "img": "modules/jjk5e/icons/techniques/blazing-courage.svg",
 "system": {
  "description": {
   "value": "<p><em>Blazing Courage — Innate Technique (1st level)</em></p><blockquote><p>Through your beliefs, you set both your weapon and heart alight with your blazing courage.</p></blockquote><p>Starting at 1st level, your technique allows yourself to ignite your weapon in flames, increasing your fire power. You can spend up to your proficiency bonus as a bonus action while holding a melee weapon, igniting said weapon in flames for 1 minute. For the duration, the weapon deals an additional 1d6 fire damage on a hit per CE spent, and emits bright light for 5 feet and dim light for another 10 feet.<br />\n This increases to 1d8 per ce spent at 6th level and again to 1d10 at 11th level and 1d12 at 18th level.</p>",
   "chat": ""
  },
